Falsifies `system_tests::user::address_space_tests::an_installed_space_stays_installed_across_a_timer_tick`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is `AddressSpace::while_installed` leaving interrupts enabled across its body, the shape
it had before 2026-10-13 (UTC). A timer tick inside the body switches to another thread on the core,
and the switch back installs the reserved root, because the scheduler records no space for a kernel
thread. The body's walk then reads the kernel's empty low half.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(seen, Some(frame), "the space was uninstalled under the body: ...")`,
with `left: None`. Confirmed red on 2026-10-13 (UTC) on all three architectures with
`cargo xtask test --arch <arch> --test an_installed_space_stays_installed_across`: x86_64 at two
cores (PVH, 4 of 4 runs) and one core (OVMF), aarch64 and riscv64 at four cores (1 of 1 each).
Replayed again on 2026-10-13 (UTC) after the precondition moved into the window (lane
maintainer/installed-space-tick-flake): red with `left: None` on riscv64 under `--cpu rva23s64` and
`--cpu thead-c906`, and on aarch64 (1 of 1 each). Re-cut on 2026-10-20 (UTC) when the `allow`
above the function changed (milestone 890 (riscv64 and `x86_64` join the shared boot path)), and
replayed red on aarch64.

diff --git a/kernel/src/user/address_space.rs b/kernel/src/user/address_space.rs
index 09742fcb1..4cebf1877 100644
--- a/kernel/src/user/address_space.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/user/address_space.rs
@@ -436,7 +436,6 @@ impl AddressSpace {
     /// (`sched::adopt_address_space`), so the switch puts it back.
     #[cfg_attr(not(feature = "system_tests"), allow(dead_code))] // the system tests are the callers
     pub fn while_installed<R>(&self, body: impl FnOnce() -> R) -> R {
-        let interrupts_were_enabled = crate::arch::interrupts::disable();
         // SAFETY: `ttbr0` composes this space's own root (built by a `Mapper` over `Half::Low`,
         // with the kernel's high half shared into it by both constructors) with the ASID allocated
         // to it, which is every architecture's contract. The root lives as long as `self`, which
@@ -445,7 +444,6 @@ impl AddressSpace {
         unsafe { mmu::activate_user(self.ttbr0()) };
         let result = body();
         mmu::deactivate_user();
-        crate::arch::interrupts::restore(interrupts_were_enabled);
         result
     }
 }
